<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at Brazil Paranagua/Santos.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at Brazil Paranagua/Santos.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping soybeans and soyproducts.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: China Hope loading 20,718 soybeans/soymeal, Agios Minas loading 54,465 tonnes soymeal, Gina loading 53,592 tonnes</p>
<p>soybeans</p>
<p>Waiting to dock: four vessels to load soymeal, one to load soybeans, two to load soybeans/meal, two to load soyoil,</p>
<p>vegetable oils</p>
<p>Road: 365 trucks carrying soybeans arrived on June 17, 390 trucks with soymeal and 70 trucks with vegetable oils including soyoil</p>
<p>Loaded (June 17): 9,114 tonnes soybeans, 35,302 tonnes soymeal Stocks: no figures available</p>
<p>SANTOS</p>
<p>Vessels: none docked</p>
<p>Waiting to dock: none</p>
<p>Road (June 17): 115 trucks unloaded 2,722 tonnes soybeans and 64 trucks unloaded 1,684 tonnes soymeal</p>
<p>Rail (June 17): 85 wagons unloaded 4,648 tonnes soybeans Loaded (June 17): 230 tonnes on the Trade Banner</p>
<p>Stocks: 91,165 tonnes soybeans, 2,933 tonnes soymeal</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
